cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "shoalkit: linear & Stokes wave transformation with theory gating"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kevin
    family-names: Griffin
    email: "thymine-coyest1d@icloud.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0439-6684"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KevinGriffin-new/shoalkit"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20904933
keywords:
  - ocean waves
  - linear wave theory
  - Stokes waves
  - dispersion relation
  - shoaling
  - refraction
  - Ursell number
  - coastal engineering
  - hydrography
abstract: >-
  A small, citable Python wrapper that solves the linear water-wave dispersion
  relation, reproduces the University of Delaware / CACR wave-calculator output
  set (wavelength, wavenumber, celerity, group velocity, direction, shoaling and
  refraction coefficients, and bottom orbital velocity), provides closed-form
  Airy and second-order Stokes surface elevation, bridges to raschii for
  higher-order Stokes and Fenton stream-function profiles, and exposes the
  Ursell number (two pinned conventions) with a transparent wave-theory
  applicability gate.
